 "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 46397, "other": 423, "system": 37262, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 21164}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 119643}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "ccc5e7d0-08b6-5a81-afd2-4a247c7fc6e4", "at": 1795685833.9193144, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86128, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "12f00fc4-7192-5978-bfed-c68a46819394", "at": 1795685835.4794514, "until": 1795685835.5264072, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86133, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (14 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "0693e6fd-ca1e-5456-948a-be79a6b22a3e", "at": 1795685835.5287542, "until": 1795685836.3809655, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86147, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01WHDniGkcjqWSjPDo5ijWj6", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git remote set-url origin \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" && timeout 90 git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; grep -n -i -E \"0\\.72|0\\.66|0\\.53|MSE|stack|cannot recover|does not recover\" Outline.md | cut -c1-500", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git remote set-url origin \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" && timeout 90 git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; grep -n -i -E \"0\\.72|0\\.66|0\\.53|MSE|stack|cannot recover|does not recover\" Outline.md | cut -c1-500"]], "output": "```console\n14:Primary endpoint (fixed before running): **RMSE ratio to uniform random sampling at n = 100 items, geometric mean over benchmarks, paired clustered bootstrap CI, per split.** One **secondary** endpoint at fixed n/N = 2% (n = 100 is ~18% of IFEval, N≈541, but <1% of MMLU-Pro, N≈12k, so the geometric mean mixes very different n/N). Conclusions must hold at both n=100 and n/N=2%, or are reported as scale-dependent. Neither is changed after seeing curves. Everything else is secondary.\n19:| C1 | **Comparison:** how do model-based, anchor-based and design-based methods rank by the primary endpoint under each split, over n from ~10 to a few hundred? | Tier-1 on all 13 benchmarks (uniform, stratified, source-calibrated regression, anchors, balanced selection with overfitting check, ours); Tier-2 as far as budget allows (tinyBenchmarks, metabench-style, kNN/low-rank, IRT-CAT); \"not run\" stated for anything not run | Fig. 2 (RMSE ratio vs n, one panel per split), Table 2 (primary e\n20:| C2 | **Bias–variance:** model-based predictors show signed bias that grows away from the source range (compression toward the source mean); the difference estimator removes it and costs a stated amount of variance — or it does not | Signed error vs true score per method class, extrapolation split especially; bias and variance computed **per target over subset draws first (≥100 draws where cheap), then summarised across targets**, with the Monte Carlo SE of each per-target bias shown (\n21:| C3 | **Factorial ablation:** a win is attributable to design, estimator, or their combination, not to a weak comparator | design {uniform, stratified, uncertainty-PPS, balanced, anchor medoids, IRT-CAT} × estimator {mean/Hájek, calibrated regression, model-based, difference}; analysis lists the **meaningful cells** (e.g. anchor medoids × difference needs weights), costs the grid, and if needed runs the full grid at the primary n only and a reduced grid across n. IRT-CAT is a **different \n22:| C4 | **Ceiling:** the gain over random sampling is bounded by how well sources predict the target's unseen items, and varies with benchmark | Per benchmark and split: the **source-only** predictor's residual-variance fraction on held-out targets' full item vectors (target answers not used); from it, the RMSE ratio the difference estimator *should* reach by the design-variance formula; observed ratio against this prediction (deviations are the finding). n/N where the finite-population correc\n62:- **If the difference estimator / design-based approach reduces RMSE over uniform and over the strongest model-based baselines in extrapolation without losing in interpolation:** the paper is a method-plus-analysis paper; headline = C2, with C4 as scope. Stated limits: positive only where the evidence says so.\n71:- **Headline (extrapolation, n = 100; selected representatives, leave-one-benchmark-out (LOBO), RMSE ratio to uniform, geometric mean over benchmarks):** *source models help most when the target resembles them. In interpolation and lineage every method class beats uniform sampling (0.65–0.72 of uniform's RMSE for the classes that use sources well, 0.80–0.94 of stratified's). For targets above the sources the gain over stratified sampling is not shown by difference correction (selected 1.0\n75:- **Main finding as the paper states it (Brief rev 5):** the source matrix buys a **limited** variance reduction, obtainable through the design (stratify or balance on source difficulty) or through the estimator (regression on the same source-side difficulty), but the two mostly do **not stack** (exception: balanced × difference with λ = 1, 0.75 vs balanced × mean 0.81 in extrapolation, both RMSE ratios to uniform × mean, a further 7% of RMSE; the MSE ratios are 0.56 and 0.66); the extra \n82:- **C5:** in extrapolation no method improves Spearman by more than ≈0.015 over uniform although RMSE improves ≈20%; ranking gains are in interpolation/lineage. Use top-decile precision (Kendal\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "0e4a9bdb-da16-517a-9a97-eb0944527599", "at": 1795685835.5741637, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86149, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "3bfe9c82-d4c4-534f-a038-bde7033aa679", "at": 1795685835.5897129, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86150, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "d135d708-6374-52f6-bb8c-f155486f90ca", "at": 1795685835.592016, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86151, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "5dedfcf8-e069-5f75-9cae-b0d5b95f4685", "at": 1795685835.8118873, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 86152, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "a5b8b289e3c3eab5b0e5970410383076", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-requi